  "version": "enrolled",
  "operative_text": "(a_in_person_id) not stated.\n(b_no_id_remedy) not stated.\n(c_mail_ballot_id) not stated.\n(d_proof_of_citizenship) not stated.\n(e_other_rule)\n(section) SECTION 1, amending S.C. Constitution Art. II, Sec. 4\n(quote) Only a citizen of the United States and of this State of the age of eighteen and upwards who is properly registered is entitled to vote as provided by law.\n(section) SECTION 2 (ballot question)\n(quote) Must Section 4, Article II of the Constitution of this State, relating to voter qualifications, be amended so as to provide that only a citizen of the United States and of this State of the age of eighteen and upwards who is properly registered is entitled to vote as provided by law?\n(other) SECTION 2: the amendment goes to the voters at the next general election for representatives (November 2024), with a yes/no ballot question.\n(other) version: 2024-02-29_Introduced: constitutional amendment so that only a citizen may vote (replaces 'Every citizen'); ballot question says 'so as to clarify that only a citizen ...'. Slots a-d: none.\n(other) version: 2024-03-27_Comm-Sub: Senate Judiciary amends the ballot question wording from 'clarify that' to 'provide that'; amendment text of Section 1 unchanged.\n(other) version: 2024-03-28_Comm-Sub: scrivener correction of the 03-27 print; same substance.\n(other) version: 2024-04-03_Comm-Sub: committee amendment adopted on the floor; ballot question now reads 'provide that'.\n(other) version: 2024-04-04_Comm-Sub: scrivener correction (title); same text.\n(other) version: 2024-04-23_Comm-Sub: House Judiciary 'favorable' with no amendment; same text as 04-04. This is the version enrolled and ratified (R 136, Act 227).\n(other) note: The saved text has NO strike/new markers at all, so in Section 1 the old word 'Every' and the new word 'Only' appear side by side ('Every  Only a citizen'). Reading: 'Every' is removed and 'Only' is added; the ratification bill S 582 (2025) prints the result as 'Only a citizen of the United States ...' and the Senate-amended ballot question says 'provide that only', which agree. id_text_in_voted_version = true here means the citizens-only qualification text is present; the bill has no ID or documentary-proof text. Joint resolution; ratified R 136 on 2024-05-08, no governor signature required. The 2024 vote of the electors is in S 582 (not in this file).\n(note) Off this topic: the bill sets no ID or citizenship-proof rule.",
  "sponsors": [],
  "single_subject": [],
